WEBVTT

00:09.970 --> 00:13.400
<i>I haven't seen Takada-kun since that day.</i>

00:14.530 --> 00:16.950
Even though we made all these plans...

00:17.370 --> 00:22.870
<b>Study\h\h\h\h\h\h\hStudy\h\h\h\h\h\h\hTakada-kun\h\h\hMountains\h\h\hStudy\h\h\h\h\h\hFestival\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hStudy\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hPool\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hStudy\h\h\h\h\h\hStudy\h\h</b>

00:17.680 --> 00:22.110
We haven't gone treasure hunting
or to any firework shows...

00:23.840 --> 00:27.190
<i>Let's play lots and lots 
during summer vacation!</i>

00:29.860 --> 00:31.400
<i>I want...</i>

00:32.690 --> 00:34.210
<i>to see Takada-kun.</i>

02:01.970 --> 02:05.980
My <b>Clueless</b> First Friend

02:07.100 --> 02:12.560
<i>Episode 5 "Call Me the Grim Reaper"</i>

02:49.920 --> 02:50.790
Ah.

02:54.170 --> 02:55.920
Takada-kun's house...

02:57.090 --> 03:00.410
<i>I ended up in front of Takada-kun's 
place before I realized it.</i>

03:01.360 --> 03:04.520
<i>What's gotten into me?</i>

03:05.160 --> 03:09.280
<i>H-He'll think I have no tact whatsoever.</i>

03:09.930 --> 03:12.140
<i>I should leave before I bother anyone...</i>

03:12.140 --> 03:12.900
Oh...

03:18.480 --> 03:20.750
T-Takada-kun...

03:21.920 --> 03:23.560
Nishimura-san.

03:30.660 --> 03:32.830
Sorry, Nishimura-san.

03:33.670 --> 03:36.870
Hino-kun and I are going to a haunted shrine
to look for will-o'-the-wisps, so...

03:36.870 --> 03:37.680
Wait!

03:46.530 --> 03:47.900
In that case...

03:47.900 --> 03:50.760
It's fine if it's just 
until Hino-kun gets here.

03:51.590 --> 03:53.340
I'm begging you...

03:53.340 --> 03:54.950
Please, let's talk.

03:56.190 --> 03:58.860
O-Okay...

04:02.900 --> 04:03.680
<i>I...</i>

04:04.560 --> 04:06.460
<i>I've done it now!</i>

04:16.190 --> 04:18.440
<i>Wh-What do I do?</i>

04:18.440 --> 04:20.550
<i>I need to say something...</i>

04:21.420 --> 04:23.540
Y-You know...

04:23.540 --> 04:25.560
I'm sorry, Nishimura-san.

04:25.560 --> 04:26.100
Huh?

04:26.490 --> 04:31.890
I won't call you the Grim Reaper anymore.

04:33.050 --> 04:34.030
What?

04:34.540 --> 04:37.120
I had no idea.

04:37.770 --> 04:40.730
That you'd lost your mom...

04:41.540 --> 04:45.060
and that you felt like you took her place.

04:46.450 --> 04:50.310
Calling you the Grim Reaper after all that...

04:50.600 --> 04:59.650
<b>Nishimura Family Grave</b>

04:50.980 --> 04:58.250
It felt like I was blaming you
 for your mom's death.

04:58.730 --> 04:59.860
And I...

05:03.840 --> 05:05.110
<i>I see.</i>

05:06.320 --> 05:09.070
<i>Takada-kun was crying back then</i>

05:09.070 --> 05:11.940
<i>because he thought he'd hurt me.</i>

05:13.800 --> 05:16.930
<i>How </i>do<i> I feel about it?</i>

05:18.560 --> 05:21.150
<i>People call me the Grim Reaper.</i>

05:22.830 --> 05:28.460
<i>When my classmates do it,
teasing me for my appearance,</i>

05:28.460 --> 05:30.570
<i>it doesn't thrill me.</i>

05:32.800 --> 05:33.730
<i>But...</i>

05:35.270 --> 05:36.600
<b>Mr. & Mrs.
 Grim Reaper</b>

05:45.270 --> 05:49.730
Hey, do you think being
a Grim Reaper is a bad thing?

05:49.730 --> 05:50.460
Huh?

05:50.920 --> 05:53.510
W-Well...

05:54.860 --> 05:57.910
Thanks for worrying about me.

05:58.350 --> 06:05.240
But you know, I don't feel bad at all 
when you call me the Grim Reaper.

06:05.670 --> 06:08.400
In fact, it makes me a little happy.

06:08.850 --> 06:12.930
I know that you're trying to 
be considerate about my mom,

06:13.240 --> 06:17.040
but that's never upset me.

06:18.620 --> 06:21.730
<i>Akane, your mother and I...</i>

06:22.170 --> 06:26.040
<i>When you came into our lives,
we were so happy.</i>

06:26.980 --> 06:29.350
<i>We're so grateful for you.</i>

06:29.350 --> 06:31.950
<i>And we always will be.</i>

06:35.120 --> 06:37.500
It's okay, Takada-kun.

06:44.030 --> 06:47.510
It's just fine by me.

06:50.830 --> 06:52.530
If my mom were here,

06:52.530 --> 06:58.430
I know she'd be happy that I made a 
friend who has a cool nickname for me.

07:00.190 --> 07:05.600
I know she'd be really glad 
that I have a friend like you.

07:06.090 --> 07:08.160
So, Takada-kun...

07:10.470 --> 07:13.870
Keep doing what you've always done...

07:14.650 --> 07:16.530
and call me the Grim Reaper!

07:20.080 --> 07:24.320
Keep using your cool nickname for me!

07:26.390 --> 07:29.110
<i>The Grim Reaper I so admired...</i>

07:30.070 --> 07:33.460
<i>is a little strange, mysterious,</i>

07:34.740 --> 07:37.740
<i>strong, and cool!</i>

07:53.010 --> 07:54.730
I-I-I'm sorry!

07:54.730 --> 07:56.680
There I go, grabbing your hands again!

07:56.680 --> 07:57.320
Eh?

07:59.970 --> 08:01.500
You didn't need to let go.

08:08.570 --> 08:10.400
I like it when we do this.

08:15.200 --> 08:19.740
I can borrow lots of your 
Grim Reaper powers like this!

08:22.450 --> 08:23.790
Takada-kun...

08:26.830 --> 08:28.740
So, Nishimura-san...

08:30.900 --> 08:35.270
Can we keep holding hands 
for a little longer?

08:35.820 --> 08:36.630
Yeah.

08:39.090 --> 08:40.310
Thanks.

08:46.030 --> 08:47.550
Oh, yeah.

08:47.550 --> 08:50.080
What about meeting up with Hino-kun?

08:50.420 --> 08:53.300
Ah! It completely slipped my mind!

08:54.170 --> 08:57.370
I wanted to play with fireworks around here!

08:57.370 --> 09:00.740
To draw out the will-o'-the-wisps 
from the haunted shrine!

09:00.740 --> 09:01.530
Eh?

09:01.910 --> 09:05.200
Are will-o'-the-wisps 
attracted to fireworks?

09:05.200 --> 09:06.860
Yo!

09:07.280 --> 09:09.570
Hino-kun! Where were you?!

09:10.180 --> 09:13.020
Looks like they're having a 
festival right around the corner.

09:13.340 --> 09:15.650
Let's go check it out 
since we're here already!

09:16.310 --> 09:18.030
That reminds me...

09:18.200 --> 09:22.160
<b>Festival</b>

09:19.010 --> 09:21.550
We put a festival on our agendas.

09:22.950 --> 09:25.860
In that case, we just have to go!

09:31.130 --> 09:35.630
<b>Takoyaki</b>

09:31.130 --> 09:35.630
<b>Shaved Ice</b>

09:31.130 --> 09:35.630
<b>Yakitori</b>

09:35.630 --> 09:44.730
<b>O
k
o
n
o
m
i
y
a
k
i</b>

09:35.630 --> 09:44.730
<b>Takoyaki</b>

09:35.630 --> 09:44.730
<b>Takoyaki</b>

09:35.630 --> 09:44.730
<b>Choco Bananas</b>

09:41.100 --> 09:42.580
Nishimura-san!

09:42.580 --> 09:43.550
C'mon, c'mon!

09:43.550 --> 09:44.740
Y-Yeah...

09:47.980 --> 09:51.270
<b>Yakisoba</b>

09:51.270 --> 09:52.890
It smells so good!

09:52.890 --> 09:53.350
I know!

09:53.350 --> 09:53.990
Let's sit and eat!

09:53.990 --> 09:55.020
Yeah, let's go!

10:03.910 --> 10:06.910
<b>Dark Matter</b>

10:03.910 --> 10:06.910
<b>Orichalcum</b>

10:37.870 --> 10:40.240
This is a blast, Nishimura-san!

10:40.820 --> 10:47.760
When I'm with you, it's way, 
way more fun than usual!

10:48.310 --> 10:49.570
<i>Takada-kun...</i>

10:49.950 --> 10:53.280
<i>I should be the one telling </i>you<i> that.</i>

10:57.090 --> 11:01.680
Thrilling Fireworks Set

10:57.960 --> 11:00.600
Hino-kun, thanks for the fireworks!

11:00.600 --> 11:01.680
I brought them from home.

11:04.060 --> 11:06.590
Hot, hot, hot!

11:04.320 --> 11:07.190
Nishimura-san, let's have 
a fireworks showdown!

11:07.540 --> 11:10.190
Whoever's lasts the longest wins!

11:10.190 --> 11:11.750
O-Okay.

11:28.000 --> 11:33.000
My <b>Clueless</b> First Friend

11:43.730 --> 11:45.500
Huh? It's gone!

11:45.500 --> 11:46.490
What?

11:46.490 --> 11:48.710
My orichalcum ring is gone!

11:48.850 --> 11:51.660
<b>Orichalcum{bottom jewelry sign}</b>

11:49.140 --> 11:51.900
It was pretty and looked powerful...

11:52.210 --> 11:56.280
So I brought it with me 
to give you as a present.

11:56.800 --> 12:00.520
O-Oh, it's fine. I don't deserve that.

12:00.520 --> 12:03.100
What? But it's made of orichalcum!

12:03.100 --> 12:05.020
Even though it only cost 120 yen...

12:05.020 --> 12:06.030
Takada-kun.

12:07.100 --> 12:08.780
Kasahara-san!

12:08.780 --> 12:12.450
Is this what you're looking for?

12:12.450 --> 12:13.360
Ah!

12:13.360 --> 12:15.480
That's the one, Kasahara-san!

12:15.480 --> 12:17.330
Thanks for finding it for me!

12:17.330 --> 12:18.900
I never said you could have it back.

12:18.900 --> 12:19.420
Huh?

12:19.760 --> 12:24.230
I'm the one who found it, so it's mine now.

12:24.230 --> 12:26.530
What? Don't say that!

12:26.530 --> 12:29.460
I was going to give it to Nishimura-san...

12:29.460 --> 12:31.530
I really don't need it.

12:33.550 --> 12:38.500
Besides, there's no way this 
ring would suit Nishimura-san.

12:38.500 --> 12:40.250
She <i>is</i> the Grim Reaper.

12:40.560 --> 12:42.020
That's true...

12:42.400 --> 12:47.050
A toy ring might be too
 low-grade for Nishimura-san.

12:47.050 --> 12:48.490
You've got it backwards, Takada-kun.

12:48.490 --> 12:50.240
You always do.

12:51.440 --> 12:54.680
You said it wouldn't suit 
Nishimura-san, right?

12:54.680 --> 12:55.700
That's right!

12:55.700 --> 12:58.100
I said it wouldn't suit Nishimura-san!

12:58.100 --> 12:59.630
This toy ring?

12:59.630 --> 13:01.220
This toy ring!

13:01.220 --> 13:05.310
In other words, I need to 
give Nishimura-san a real ring!

13:05.310 --> 13:06.920
How'd you get to that?!

13:07.520 --> 13:10.470
I'm sorry, though, Nishimura-san.

13:10.470 --> 13:13.480
Oh, you had another ring.

13:13.480 --> 13:18.600
I'm still just a kid, so I can't get 
you anything better than a toy ring.

13:18.600 --> 13:21.610
N-No... That's not...

13:22.590 --> 13:25.900
By the way, that one's a dark matter ring!

13:25.900 --> 13:30.990
It absorbs dark magic, so maybe it 
suits you better than orichalcum!

13:31.320 --> 13:34.280
Y-Yeah. Thanks...

13:35.410 --> 13:38.390
Thanks to all of you 
for your advice, as well!

13:38.390 --> 13:39.780
That is <i>not</i> what happened!

13:50.010 --> 13:54.850
<i>I'm still just a kid, so I can't get 
you anything better than a toy ring.</i>

13:56.240 --> 14:00.380
Even a toy ring is more 
than enough to make me happy.

14:00.980 --> 14:03.400
I'll cherish it as a precious treasure.

14:12.070 --> 14:13.260
Nishimura-san.

14:15.340 --> 14:17.950
I have an important favor to ask.

14:17.950 --> 14:20.460
What's this all of a sudden?

14:22.430 --> 14:25.350
Do you mind if I tickle you a little?

14:26.050 --> 14:27.800
Wh-Why?!

14:27.800 --> 14:29.960
Th-That's embarrassing, so no!

14:30.840 --> 14:32.560
I see...

14:32.770 --> 14:35.570
Sorry for asking something so weird.

14:36.600 --> 14:38.550
I-I don't mind.

14:38.810 --> 14:40.560
But why do you want to do that?

14:40.970 --> 14:41.810
Oh.

14:41.810 --> 14:48.770
Is it because everyone in class says you'll 
be cursed if the Grim Reaper smiles upon you?

14:48.770 --> 14:49.420
What?

14:50.110 --> 14:52.360
No, you've got totally the wrong idea.

14:52.360 --> 14:53.930
<i>I had totally the wrong idea!</i>

14:53.930 --> 14:55.820
<i>An unexpected new pattern!</i>

14:57.190 --> 15:03.320
I haven't seen you laugh a lot, 
so I was wondering if you ever cracked up.

15:03.860 --> 15:06.740
Anyway, I never knew you
could curse with a smile!

15:06.740 --> 15:07.960
That's incredible!

15:07.960 --> 15:10.160
I-I wouldn't know...

15:10.160 --> 15:12.540
That's just what some people say.

15:12.990 --> 15:18.350
A-Also, I can laugh just fine,
even without being tickled.

15:18.350 --> 15:19.410
Really?!

15:19.410 --> 15:21.350
Then I'll try my best!

15:21.350 --> 15:22.600
Try your best?

15:23.470 --> 15:27.430
I'll get your curse if you smile at me, right?

15:28.110 --> 15:30.740
I can't say whether that's true or not...

15:35.080 --> 15:41.130
I might as well try and become the person 
who can make you smile the most.

15:46.070 --> 15:49.510
I want you to smile lots 
when you're with me!

15:51.710 --> 15:56.390
<i>If you say that, I'll break 
out into a grin again!</i>

15:56.390 --> 15:57.270
Huh?

15:57.270 --> 15:59.100
Wait, are you smiling right now?

16:01.260 --> 16:03.890
If you're gonna smile, then show me!

16:03.890 --> 16:06.440
Ah, w-wait...

16:06.440 --> 16:10.290
Curse me, or else you're 
just doing it to be cute!

16:10.290 --> 16:11.540
Takada-kun!

16:11.540 --> 16:14.500
Hey, look at me, Nishimura-san!

16:16.240 --> 16:19.240
<b>That-There Park</b>

16:19.670 --> 16:22.070
A photo contest?

16:22.410 --> 16:24.700
The department store nearby is running it!

16:24.700 --> 16:27.920
The first-place winner gets a music player!

16:27.920 --> 16:29.870
I-Is that right?

16:30.510 --> 16:33.540
Can I take a few photos
of you while I'm at it?

16:33.840 --> 16:35.590
Huh? Of me?!

16:35.590 --> 16:38.650
I don't think there's any merit 
in photographing me...

16:38.650 --> 16:41.550
What? You think so?

16:41.550 --> 16:45.510
I thought it'd make for 
some awesome photos...

16:45.910 --> 16:47.610
<i>Awesome?</i>

16:47.610 --> 16:50.800
Is there any other awesome stuff around here?

16:50.800 --> 16:53.320
W-Want me to help you look?

16:53.320 --> 16:54.930
Really? Are you sure?

16:54.930 --> 16:55.680
Yeah.

16:55.680 --> 16:56.900
Heck yeah!

16:56.900 --> 17:01.720
I'll snap loads of photos today
and make sure to win first place!

17:01.720 --> 17:03.550
Y-Yeah!

17:10.660 --> 17:11.750
<i>Huh?</i>

17:11.750 --> 17:14.320
<i>He's still taking photos of me.</i>

17:14.320 --> 17:16.520
Hmm, that's no good.

17:16.520 --> 17:18.670
Your outfit's too cute today.

17:19.140 --> 17:21.420
I want to take an awesome photo,

17:21.420 --> 17:25.320
but your cuteness overpowers it,
so it doesn't read as cool.

17:26.150 --> 17:28.680
I need a more awesome photo!

17:28.960 --> 17:32.340
Nishimura-san, do you have any good ideas?

17:32.340 --> 17:33.960
Huh? Ah...

17:34.670 --> 17:38.150
Wh-Why don't you ask Hino-kun, as well?

17:38.570 --> 17:41.580
<b>That-There Shopping District</b>

17:38.570 --> 17:41.580
<b>That-There Boutique</b>

17:38.570 --> 17:41.580
<b>Alcohol</b>

17:41.970 --> 17:44.070
Ta... Tan...

17:44.070 --> 17:45.500
He says tank tops!

17:45.500 --> 17:47.450
I figured he would.

17:47.450 --> 17:49.600
Tank... tops...

17:48.200 --> 17:52.030
A-Anyway, you should try taking 
pictures of lots of things.

17:52.030 --> 17:53.120
You're right!

17:58.250 --> 17:59.380
Yay!

17:58.250 --> 17:59.380
Yo!

17:58.260 --> 18:01.010
<b>Candy Shop</b>

18:06.200 --> 18:06.960
Ah!

18:06.960 --> 18:08.920
Let's go, Nishimura-san!

18:14.570 --> 18:19.110
<b>That-There Drugstore</b>

18:14.850 --> 18:16.670
Found a monster!

18:16.670 --> 18:19.110
Nishimura-san, take a photo! Hurry!

18:22.110 --> 18:24.050
D-Don't move.

18:24.050 --> 18:24.570
Huh?

18:24.570 --> 18:26.060
Did you say something?

18:35.050 --> 18:36.420
Hino-kun...

19:20.190 --> 19:22.100
We sure took lots of pictures, huh?

19:22.100 --> 19:23.420
Y-Yeah.

19:23.790 --> 19:26.910
I've made tons of memories this summer.

19:27.990 --> 19:29.950
Thanks, Nishimura-san.

19:29.950 --> 19:30.640
What?

19:30.640 --> 19:36.100
This summer vacation was really 
fun because you hung out with me.

19:38.560 --> 19:40.500
Hey, what about me?

19:41.510 --> 19:43.980
You too, of course, Hino-kun!

19:44.850 --> 19:48.600
<i>Summer vacation was so much fun...</i>

19:49.370 --> 19:55.130
<i>That really should be my line, Takada-kun.</i>

19:50.330 --> 19:53.690
<b>Candy Shop</b>

19:57.880 --> 20:00.840
<b>Sporting Goods</b>

19:57.880 --> 20:00.840
Sneakers

19:57.880 --> 20:00.840
Sales, Popular Products

20:00.840 --> 20:04.890
<b>Photo Contest</b>

20:04.890 --> 20:10.980
<b>Second Place</b>

21:48.160 --> 21:49.930
I'm so bored...

21:52.500 --> 21:56.200
<i>I wonder what Nishimura-san's up to.</i>

21:56.570 --> 22:00.740
<i>For some reason,
 I can't stop thinking about her lately.</i>

22:01.320 --> 22:04.260
<i>I guess she's just that interesting!</i>

22:04.260 --> 22:05.890
Get a load of that grin.

22:06.780 --> 22:08.750
Something good happen to you?

22:09.300 --> 22:11.950
Huh? I was grinning?

22:11.950 --> 22:13.300
I wonder why.

22:13.620 --> 22:18.200
Hmm, I bet you were thinking 
about Nishimura-san.

22:18.200 --> 22:20.330
What?! That's amazing!

22:20.330 --> 22:22.810
How did you know, Onee-chan?

22:22.810 --> 22:27.930
I couldn't think of any other reason
 you'd look so over the moon.

22:28.280 --> 22:31.570
D-Did I really look that happy?

22:31.570 --> 22:33.050
You totally did.

22:33.050 --> 22:36.850
I mean, Nishimura-san <i>is</i> an angel.

22:36.850 --> 22:37.750
An angel?!

22:38.180 --> 22:42.540
A Grim Reaper <i>and</i> an angel?!
Nishimura-san's way too powerful!

22:42.540 --> 22:46.420
She's got a Dual Skill, 
rarely found even in Skill Holders!

22:46.420 --> 22:50.390
I don't know about this Grim Reaper stuff, 
but I'm dead serious about the angel part.

22:50.600 --> 22:52.790
She's cute enough that she seriously is one.

22:52.790 --> 22:54.890
She's cute enough 
hat she's seriously an angel?!

22:54.890 --> 23:00.090
But Nishimura-san doesn't 
seem to realize it...

23:00.090 --> 23:01.350
That's so sad!

23:01.350 --> 23:02.900
I need to tell her!

23:04.000 --> 23:06.100
What's up, Takada-kun?

23:06.100 --> 23:08.640
You seem to be having more fun than usual.

23:08.640 --> 23:10.460
You think so?

23:10.460 --> 23:13.080
Maybe it's because I'm with you.

23:13.080 --> 23:14.040
What?

23:14.040 --> 23:18.040
Nishimura-san, maybe you
 haven't realized this about yourself,

23:18.680 --> 23:22.350
but you're really an angel.

23:22.350 --> 23:24.080
Huh? Huh?!

23:24.080 --> 23:26.880
You're so cute! Seriously an angel!

23:26.880 --> 23:27.600
What?

23:27.600 --> 23:28.940
What?!

23:28.940 --> 23:31.830
Your blushing is also seriously angelic!

23:34.970 --> 23:39.970
<b>Next time...</b>

23:34.970 --> 23:39.970
<b>Changing Desks, Class Reps, and New Friends</b>
